<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cerdic</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cerdic of Wessex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cerdic is named by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxon-chronicle">Anglo-Saxon Chronicle</a> as the founder of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>. It says he landed in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cynric">Cynric</a> in 495 and took the kingship in 519, ruling until 534, and later West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> kings traced their descent from him. His name appears to be of British rather than English origin, and historians treat the Chronicle's account as largely legendary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cerdic.jpg" alt="Cerdic" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cherdik_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
